+### Compound Format
+
+Set `compound: true` to output multiple units, largest first.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h 30m"
+ms(90061000, { compound: true })      // "1d 1h 1m 1s"
+ms(3601999, { compound: true })       // "1h 1s"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h 30m"
+```
+
+Notes:
+
+- Zero parts are skipped, and the largest unit is days (`8 * 86400000` is `"8d"`).
+- The smallest unit is seconds; leftover milliseconds are dropped, so values under one second give `"0s"`.
+- Only applies to the short format. If `long: true` is also set, `long` takes precedence.
+
